1a. Ready-made firmware images (.bin files)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section applies to anybody who passes on a compiled firmware image of this project
(for example a .bin file attached to a release). It is not legal advice; it only repeats what
the sources named here say. Check the licence texts themselves before you publish an image.

- The image contains the Arduino core for ESP32 (LGPL-2.1-or-later). LGPL-2.1 asks a
  distributor of a binary to pass on the licence text and to make it possible for the
  recipient to rebuild or relink the program with a changed version of the library. This
  project publishes its complete source code, the pinned versions of the platform and packages
  (firmware/platformio.ini) and the build instructions (docs/en/quick-start/flash.md), so any
  image can be rebuilt from the same sources. A release with images should also include, or
  point to, the LGPL-2.1 text and the source of the exact arduino-esp32 version used
  (https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32, release 3.3.12).
- The image contains parts of ESP-IDF. ESP-IDF's own source code is under Apache-2.0; ESP-IDF
  also includes third-party components under other licences (for example BSD, MIT and
  Apache-2.0 components), each with its own notices. The list for the ESP-IDF version used
  here is on Espressif's page "Copyrights and Licenses":
  https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v5.5.5/esp32s3/COPYRIGHT.html
  Which of these components end up in an image depends on the build; a release with images
  should carry the notices that page asks for.
- When the pinned platform or package versions change, update the versions in this section.

