3. Data sources
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PSA-RE, https://github.com/prototux/PSA-RE (Apache-2.0), commit 67f7581e
  Community descriptions of PSA CAN frames. This project uses them only as "unverified"
  descriptions, with a link and the path inside PSA-RE (for example
  buses/AEE2010.full/LS.INFO-DIV/364.yml), next to its own measurements, which are marked
  "measured". Its files are not copied into this repository.

Most other facts about the car, the radio and the CAN boxes come from the author's own
measurements and recordings (firmware/test_data/captures). Every protocol constant in the
firmware has its source in radios/xp-simple-soft/provenance.md (state of 2026-11-19: 109
constants, 108 measured, 1 design choice, none marked "source: firmware analysis / needs owner
decision"). The constants that had no own measurement were measured in the session of
2026-11-19 (38) or removed from the code (33: the bits of frame 364 with the climate trial, the
language codes other than Polish, three vehicle setting numbers, the radio frame C5, one sound
row and the Stop and Start content of frame 1A9). A few bits of the frames sent to the radio
(listed as "unverified" in the same file) agree with the recordings but never changed in them;
they decide only what the radio screen shows. Two other public projects (one under GPL-3.0) were
read to understand frame 1A9; nothing was copied from them, and the 1A9 content known only from
them (Stop and Start) is not in the firmware.

